As the Operations Chair for PFLAG Los Angeles, I designed and delivered a live workshop via Zoom on cybersecurity best practices and introduced the new cybersecurity policies. See the presentation in Canva.

Cybersecurity Essentials: Safeguarding PFLAG Los Angeles

In a follow-up email, I included a summary of action items and a handout: 8 Habits to Stay Cyber-Safe.
8 Habits to Stay Cyber-Safe hand out

Instructional Design Methods Used: SAM, Universal Design for Learning (UDL)
Audience: Non-Profit Board Members with limited-to-average technical knowledge.
Learning Objectives: By the end of the training, learners will be able to:
Recognize red flags in phishing emails/messages.
Implement strong password practices, including using strong, unique passwords and 2FA/MFA.
Summarize the importance of immediately updating software to patch vulnerabilities.
Demonstrate the steps to take if there’s a security incident.
